data: {"text":"1. That the above-named applicant has been falsely implicated in FIR No. 124/2026 dated 15/03/2026,"}

data: {"text":" registered at Police Station Kotwali, under Sections 303 and 351 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023,"}

data: {"text":" and has been languishing in judicial custody since his arrest on 16/03/2026.\n\n2. That the present case"}

data: {"text":" against the applicant has arisen out of a civil dispute pertaining to land ownership between"}

data: {"text":" the applicant and the complainant, which has been deliberately given a criminal color to har"}

data: {"text":"ass and intimidate the applicant. The complainant, being unable to succeed in the civil proceedings"}

data: {"text":", has resorted to filing false criminal allegations against the applicant.\n\n3. That the applicant was not present at the place of the alleged incident at"}

data: {"text":" the time when it is purported to have occurred. The applicant has credible witnesses who"}

data: {"text":" can substantiate his whereabouts during the relevant time, thereby establishing a complete alibi in"}

data: {"text":" his favor. The applicant was at his workplace and can"}

data: {"text":" produce documentary evidence and witness testimony to prove the same.\n\n4. That the applicant has been fals"}

data: {"text":"ely implicated in the present case due to the ulterior motives of the complainant who seeks to settle scores"}

data: {"text":" arising from the ongoing land dispute. The allegations leveled against the applicant are completely baseless,"}

data: {"text":" fabricated, and without any merit whatsoever.\n\n5. That the applicant is a law-abiding citizen with"}

data: {"text":" deep roots in the community and has no propensity to flee from justice. He has full faith"}

data: {"text":" in the judicial system and is committed to facing the trial and proving"}

data: {"text":" his innocence. The applicant has a permanent residence, stable employment, and family ties in the locality"}

data: {"text":", which eliminate any possibility of him absconding.\n\n6. That the applicant has no previous"}

data: {"text":" criminal antecedents and has never been involved in any criminal activity. His conduct has always been exemplary, and he enjoys a good"}

data: {"text":" reputation in society. This being his first brush with the criminal justice system, he deserves the"}

data: {"text":" benefit of liberal consideration for bail.\n\n7. That the applicant has been fully cooperating with the investigation and has appeared before the investigating authorities whenever"}

data: {"text":" called upon. He has not tampered with any evidence nor influenced any witnesses, and there"}

data: {"text":" is no apprehension of him doing so in the future.\n\n8. That the continued detention of the applicant in judicial custody would serve no useful purpose as"}

data: {"text":" the investigation has been completed and the chargesheet has been filed. The applicant's further inc"}

data: {"text":"arceration would amount to punishment before trial, which is contrary to the established principles"}

data: {"text":" of criminal jurisprudence.\n\n9. That the fundamental right to life and personal liberty guaranteed"}

data: {"text":" under Article 21 of the Constitution of India includes the right to bail, and the same cannot be denied arbitrarily. The applicant has"}

data: {"text":" been in custody for a considerable period, and his continued detention without bail"}

data: {"text":" would be a violation of his constitutional rights.\n\n10. That considering the nature of the allegations, the evidence on record, and the fact that the applicant poses no threat"}

data: {"text":" to society or the investigation, this Hon'ble Court may be pleased to exercise"}

data: {"text":" its discretionary power under Section 479 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, and grant bail to the applicant on such terms"}

data: {"text":" and conditions as deemed fit."}

